      <p class="/_attributes/common-attributes.md"></p>
      <p>With OpenShift Container Platform 4.22, a docker socket will not be present on the host nodes. This means the <em>mount docker socket</em> option of a custom build is not guaranteed to provide an accessible docker socket for use within a custom build image.</p>
      <p>If you require this capability in order to build and push images, add the Buildah tool your custom build image and use it to build and push the image within your custom build logic. The following is an example of how to run custom builds with Buildah.</p>
